      <div type="clause" n="22">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 22</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="xno" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="510–511" ed="#liebermann"/>Ki Franceis ocist, e les humes del hundred nel prengent e meinent a la justise<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#LeisWl_22.lnote.oe.1"/> dedenz les VIII jurs<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#LeisWl_22.lnote.oe.2"/>, pur mustrer, ki<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="a" target="#LeisWl_22.lnote.oe.a"/> l'ait fet, si renderunt le murdre: XLVI mars.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="xno" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-i"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#LeisWl_22.lnote.oe.1-2"/><pb n="510–511" ed="#liebermann"/>De<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="a" target="#LeisWl_22.lnote.oe.a-2"/> murdre. Ki<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#LeisWl_22.lnote.oe.2-2"/> Fre[n]ceis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#LeisWl_22.lnote.oe.3"/> occist, e les homes del hundred nel prengent e amenent a la justise dedenz les oit jours, pur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#LeisWl_22.lnote.oe.4"/> mustrer, pur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="a" target="#LeisWl_22.lnote.oe.a-2"/> qui il l'a fait, si'n rendrunt le murdre: XLVII<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="b" target="#LeisWl_22.lnote.oe.b"/> mars.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-l"><pb n="510–511" ed="#liebermann"/>De murdre. Si quis Francum hominem occiderit, et non capiant homines de uisneto occisorem infra ebdomadam et offerant iusticiariis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="a" target="#LeisWl_22.lnote.oe.a-3"/> ad ostendendum, quamobrem hoc ille fecerit, reddent pro murdre XLVII m.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="22" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="264" ed="#robertson"/>Ki Franceis ocist, e les humes del hundred nel prengent e meinent a la justise dedenz les VIII jurs pur mustrer ki l'ait fet, si renderunt le murdre: XLVI mars.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="510–511" ed="#liebermann"/>22. (Vom Murdrum. <hi rend="italic">IL</hi>) Wer [= Wenn jemand] einen Franzosen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#LeisWl_22.lnote.de.1"/> tödtet, gesetzt dass die Leute des Hundred<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#missing"/> ihn nicht verhaften<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#missing"/> und vor Gericht führen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#LeisWl_22.lnote.de.4"/> binnen 8 Tagen, um [also] zu erweisen, wer (warum er <hi rend="italic">IL</hi>) es gethan habe, so sollen sie (dafür <hi rend="italic">IL</hi>) die Murdrum[busse] zahlen: 46 (47 <hi rend="italic">IL</hi>) Mark [30²/₃ £].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">22. (Of murdrum. <hi rend="italic">IL</hi>) Whoever [= If someone] kills a Frenchman, supposing that the people of the hundred do not arrest him and bring him before the court within 8 days, in order [thus] to show who (why he <hi rend="italic">IL</hi>) did it, then they shall pay (for it <hi rend="italic">IL</hi>) the murdrum [fine]: 46 (47 <hi rend="italic">IL</hi>) marks [30²/₃ £].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="265" ed="#robertson"/>If a Frenchman is slain and the men of the hundred do not seize the slayer and bring him to court within 8 days, in order to prove who has done it, they shall pay the murder-fine, namely 46 marks.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="511"><ref target="clause:WlArt_3">Wl art 3</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">vgl. Wl art. 3</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="409"><label>influenced by</label> <ref target="clause:WlArt_3">Wl art 3</ref> <quote>the 'Articles' seem to influence only the clauses on murdrum and perhaps frankpledge</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="409"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Hn_91-1">Hn 91.1</ref> <quote>the former allows eight days' grace against Wl art. 3's five (and Hn 91:1's seven)</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 264–265 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text and German translation added from Gesetze I p. 510–511, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_22.lnote.oe.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">510</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">k'il <hi rend="italic">TO.;</hi> k'il l'ait <hi rend="italic">ändert MAT.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">k'il TO.; altered to k'il l'ait by MAT.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_22.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">510</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ice <hi rend="italic">ändert TO.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ice altered by TO.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_22.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">510</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">jurz <hi rend="italic">ändert TO.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">jurz altered by TO.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_22.lnote.oe.a-2" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">510</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so auch L</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">so also L</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_22.lnote.oe.b" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">510</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so auch L, bessere</hi> 46</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">so also L; read 46</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_22.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">510</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">XXVI. <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">XXVI. I</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_22.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">510</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">missing in Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_22.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">510</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Freceis <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Freceis I</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_22.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">510</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">per <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">per Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_22.lnote.oe.a-3" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">511</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">L denkt an königliches Colleg, wohl der Reiserichter, wie</hi> 17, 3. 31</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">L has in mind a royal body of judges, probably the itinerant justices, as in 17, 3. 31</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_22.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">289</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Murdrum 6. Auch Lothringer in des Eroberers Gefolge sind mitgemeint. <hi rend="italic">S. o</hi>. S. 280 Sp. 2</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Murdrum 6. Lorrainers in the Conqueror’s following are also included. <hi rend="italic">See above</hi> p. 280 col. 2</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_22.lnote.de.2__3" n="2. 3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">289</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Ebd</hi>. 10b. 11f; Hundred 21b. Mit ‘Nachbarschaft’ meint L wohl Dorf (<hi rend="italic">s. d</hi>. 7e) oder wie 21, 5 drei Nachbardörfer</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Ibid</hi>. 10b. 11f; Hundred 21b. By ‘neighbourhood’ L probably means the village (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word 7e) or, as in 21, 5, three neighbouring villages</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_22.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">289</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Viell. wird L benutzt durch <hi rend="italic">Dial. de scacc</hi>. I 10 ed. Hughes p. 99: <hi rend="italic">festinaret quisque . . offerre iudicio</hi> den Schadenstifter für <hi rend="italic">viciniam</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Perhaps L is used by <hi rend="italic">Dial. de scacc</hi>. I 10 ed. Hughes p. 99: <hi rend="italic">festinaret quisque . . offerre iudicio</hi> the wrongdoer, in place of <hi rend="italic">viciniam</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_22.lnote.de.5__6" n="5. 6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">289</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. Gl</hi> Murdrum 9a. 14</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See Gl</hi> Murdrum 9a. 14</seg></note>
      </div>
